      "lang": "en",
      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "CGI versions before 5.00 for Perl trust the client X-Forwarded-Host header in url, self_url, virtual_host and virtual_port.\n\nThese take the host name and port from the X-Forwarded-Host request header when present, and otherwise from Host, without validating either. The URLs from url and self_url are the default redirect location and the start_html(-base=>1) base href, and the default start_form action when REQUEST_URI is not set.\n\nA client can poison shared caches, and URLs the application stores or sends, with redirects, links and scripts that point at a host it controls.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
      ],
